{"title":"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems\">2001 AMC 12 #10</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems\">2001 AMC 10 #18</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The plane is tiled by congruent squares and congruent pentagons as indicated. The percent of the plane that is enclosed by the pentagons is closest to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c8743395e4a086d2ae9a30a2d161157e7dc3077.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(3mm); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8pt));  path p1=(0,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3)--(0,0); path p2=(0,1)--(1,1)--(1,0); path p3=(2,0)--(2,1)--(3,1); path p4=(3,2)--(2,2)--(2,3); path p5=(1,3)--(1,2)--(0,2); path p6=(1,1)--(2,2); path p7=(2,1)--(1,2); path[] p=p1^^p2^^p3^^p4^^p5^^p6^^p7; for(int i=0; i&lt;3; ++i) { for(int j=0; j&lt;3; ++j) { draw(shift(3*i,3*j)*p); } } [/asy]\" width=\"132\" height=\"132\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c03670acfda2d0da15624f2952ca42a51e2d50b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }50 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }52  \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }54 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }56 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }58$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider any single tile:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f7a20120732a8955c3f77ea0d1e81fc34cc6ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1cm); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8pt));  path p1=(0,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3)--(0,0); path p2=(0,1)--(1,1)--(1,0); path p3=(2,0)--(2,1)--(3,1); path p4=(3,2)--(2,2)--(2,3); path p5=(1,3)--(1,2)--(0,2); path p6=(1,1)--(2,2); path p7=(2,1)--(1,2); path[] p=p1^^p2^^p3^^p4^^p5^^p6^^p7; draw(p); [/asy]\" width=\"145\" height=\"145\" />\n</p><p>If the side of the small square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, then the area of the tile is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/593bc7544dfb566df6afd3e6218f9f6db2e3b400.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(3a\\right)^2 = 9a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"23\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/4/3a44703d1e5cfe85d058cecef2cf6f399d432a97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> covered by squares, and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/6/0c676c26202edfc7344300377ac43d86536e98fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9a^2-4a^2 = 5a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" /> by pentagons.\nHence exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7cee4c1bc083c3979f7ac19ac9f8646a3d0a29e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of any tile is covered by pentagons, and therefore pentagons cover <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7cee4c1bc083c3979f7ac19ac9f8646a3d0a29e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of the plane. When expressed as a percentage, this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/7/f976960274554321717300463c44555b12ea4447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55.\\overline{5}\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" />, and the closest integer to this value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f30c094effce728b683f045ce82e98c1f33266d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }56}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> smaller square tiles on each side of the bigger square. We are double counting the four corner tiles, however, so we subtract by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Additionally, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inner square inside each hole of the two 8 looking figures inside the square. Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />*<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />*<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inner squares. Thus, there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> squares. Because we are dealing with percentages, and therefore fractions and ratios, we can set the side length to anything we want as long as we maintain consistency throughout the entire figure. For simplicity sake, we set the side length of each small square to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the side length of the big square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Because the amount of squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the total area of all the small squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The area of the big square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />*<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/e/04ee9ab131041bd6e87ffe78186a0f13e38a8af1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{36}{81}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/b/14bd331780e3aa8eb581193b53ca357bfae6f21d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of the entire figure is covered by squares. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7cee4c1bc083c3979f7ac19ac9f8646a3d0a29e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> is covered by pentagons. Expressed as a decimal, this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/7/f976960274554321717300463c44555b12ea4447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55.\\overline{5}\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" />. The closest percent value to this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f30c094effce728b683f045ce82e98c1f33266d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }56}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P43NYTbZH4k\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P43NYTbZH4k</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12\" title=\"2001 AMC 12\">2001 AMC 12</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?titl